<article class="env-lemma" id="00IG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00IG">Lemma <span data-tag="00IG">10.50.16</span>.</a> Let $(\Gamma , \geq )$ be a totally ordered abelian group. Let $K$ be a field. Let $v : K^* \to \Gamma $ be a homomorphism of abelian groups such that $v(a + b) \geq \min (v(a), v(b))$ for $a, b \in K$ with $a, b, a + b$ not zero. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A = \{  x \in K \mid x = 0 \text{ or } v(x) \geq 0 \}   \]
</div>
  <p> is a valuation ring with value group $\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(v) \subset \Gamma $, with maximal ideal </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathfrak m = \{  x \in K \mid x = 0 \text{ or } v(x) > 0 \}   \]
</div>
  <p> and with group of units </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A^* = \{  x \in K^* \mid v(x) = 0 \} .  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>